WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:21.469
The next morning Little Joe and Merrylegs left for the minister's house.

2
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:26.695
Then John saddled Ginger and mounted, leading me beside her.

3
00:00:26.696 --> 00:00:32.044
We rode out through the gates of Birtwick Park without looking back.

4
00:00:32.045 --> 00:00:36.320
After about fifteen miles we came to a place called Earlshall Park.

5
00:00:36.321 --> 00:00:39.690
This would be our new home.

6
00:00:39.691 --> 00:00:45.106
The estate had a very fancy house and a large stable.

7
00:00:45.107 --> 00:00:50.018
When we reached the stableyard, John asked for Mr. York.

8
00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:55.623
York was the man in charge of the earl's stable, horses, and carriages.

9
00:00:55.624 --> 00:01:00.418
He was a handsome man with a manner that said he expected to be obeyed.

10
00:01:00.419 --> 00:01:06.255
"It's nice to meet you," he said to John. "Thanks for delivering the new horses."

11
00:01:06.256 --> 00:01:09.978
He called for the grooms to take Ginger and me inside.

12
00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:13.818
Then he invited John to come and have some tea.

13
00:01:13.819 --> 00:01:18.951
The grooms led us into the bright, airy stable.

14
00:01:18.952 --> 00:01:27.539
One led me into a large, deeply bedded stall, and the other took Ginger into the equally nice stall beside it.

15
00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:30.924
Then they groomed us and gave us some hay.

16
00:01:30.925 --> 00:01:37.738
Half an hour later John and Mr. York returned. York looked us over carefully.

17
00:01:37.739 --> 00:01:42.686
"These look like very nice horses, Mr. Manly," he said to John.

18
00:01:42.687 --> 00:01:45.569
"Is there anything you'd like to tell me about them?

19
00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.776
All horses have their quirks."

20
00:01:48.777 --> 00:01:53.746
"I don't believe there's a better pair of horses in the country," John replied.

21
00:01:53.747 --> 00:01:58.649
"I'm very sorry to part with them. But you should know that they're not alike.

22
00:01:58.650 --> 00:02:02.491
The black one has the most perfect nature I've ever seen.

23
00:02:02.492 --> 00:02:08.380
I don't think he's ever known a harsh word or an unfair punishment since he was foaled."

24
00:02:08.381 --> 00:02:11.208
"Excellent," York said.

25
00:02:11.209 --> 00:02:15.394
"But the chestnut one hasn't been so lucky," John went on.

26
00:02:15.395 --> 00:02:20.336
"We bought her from a dealer who said she'd had some bad treatment in her early years.

27
00:02:20.337 --> 00:02:23.879
When we got her, she was tense and suspicious.

28
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:29.925
But after some good handling at our place, she relaxed, and for the past three years she's been very good."

29
00:02:29.926 --> 00:02:32.365
"I see," York said.

30
00:02:32.366 --> 00:02:36.880
"If she's well-treated, there isn't a better, more willing animal," John said.

31
00:02:36.881 --> 00:02:39.274
"But she's still high-strung.

32
00:02:39.275 --> 00:02:44.942
She's more bothered by flies than most horses, and likely to be annoyed by the harness too.

33
00:02:44.943 --> 00:02:49.556
If she were unfairly treated, she'd probably react strongly."

34
00:02:49.557 --> 00:02:53.846
"Many spirited horses are like that," York said with a nod.

35
00:02:53.847 --> 00:02:59.244
"Thank you for the information, Mr. Manly. I'll remember what you've told me."

36
00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:03.128
"Oh, I almost forgot to mention one more thing," John said.

37
00:03:03.129 --> 00:03:07.817
"We've never used the checkrein to hold up the head of either of these horses.

38
00:03:07.818 --> 00:03:13.303
The black horse has never worn one in his life, and the dealer said it's what spoiled the mare."

39
00:03:13.304 --> 00:03:18.061
"Well, they're going to have to wear it here, I'm afraid," York said.

40
00:03:18.062 --> 00:03:23.032
"I prefer a loose rein myself, and the earl doesn't care.

41
00:03:23.033 --> 00:03:27.891
But the lady is very interested in style and fashion.

42
00:03:27.892 --> 00:03:33.277
If her carriage horses aren't reined up tight, she won't even look at them."

43
00:03:33.278 --> 00:03:37.134
"I'm sorry to hear that," John said with a sigh.

44
00:03:37.135 --> 00:03:40.411
"But I'd better go, or I'll miss my train."

45
00:03:40.412 --> 00:03:42.815
John stepped into my stall.

46
00:03:42.816 --> 00:03:47.026
"Good-bye, you two," he said, giving Ginger and me each a pat.

47
00:03:47.027 --> 00:03:49.513
"I hope you'll be happy here."

48
00:03:49.514 --> 00:03:51.410
His voice sounded sad.

49
00:03:51.411 --> 00:03:56.432
All I could do to say good-bye was hold my face close to him.

50
00:03:56.433 --> 00:04:02.726
Soon he was gone, and to this day I've never seen him since.

51
00:04:02.727 --> 00:04:08.563
The next day the earl came to look at us. He seemed pleased by what he saw.

52
00:04:08.564 --> 00:04:13.229
"These horses are just as nice as squire said," he commented.

53
00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:19.074
"It's too bad they're not a match in color, but they'll be fine for driving around the countryside."

54
00:04:19.075 --> 00:04:23.699
York agreed. Then he told the earl what John had said about us.

55
00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:27.182
"Hmm." The earl glanced at Ginger.

56
00:04:27.183 --> 00:04:31.273
"Keep an eye on the mare, and start with the checkrein loose.

57
00:04:31.274 --> 00:04:36.317
If you tighten it up a little at a time, I'm sure they'll both get used to it soon.

58
00:04:36.318 --> 00:04:39.478
I'll mention it to my wife."

59
00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:43.740
That afternoon the grooms harnessed us to a fine carriage.

60
00:04:43.741 --> 00:04:47.341
For the first time I had the checkrein attached to my bridle.

61
00:04:47.342 --> 00:04:51.238
It was strange not to be able to lower my head if I wished.

62
00:04:51.239 --> 00:04:55.683
But my head wasn't held any higher than normal, so I didn't mind too much.

63
00:04:55.684 --> 00:04:58.442
Ginger didn't complain either.

64
00:04:58.443 --> 00:05:04.630
As the clock struck three, we were led around to the front of the house.

65
00:05:04.631 --> 00:05:10.046
With a rustling of silk, a proud-looking lady walked down the steps to meet us.

66
00:05:10.047 --> 00:05:12.503
She looked at Ginger and me and frowned.

67
00:05:12.504 --> 00:05:19.462
But she said nothing—at least not on that first day.
